WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.820
Russian missiles killed one person in Kiev hours after a U.S. envoy met Putin. This is Omni View, episode

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:11.860
213. Fighting in Yemen, an airport attack in Saudi Arabia and Germany's economic overhaul

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:17.800
come next. Then understanding the issue. Ukrainian officials reported 22 people injured in the

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:23.840
capital from ballistic missiles, and Al Jazeera recorded president Volodymyr Zelensky, describing

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:29.460
the attackers as Russian humanitarians. That dispatch treated the bombardment as an escalation

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.700
and framed Ukrainian resistance as a refusal to accept appeasement, with harm to civilians

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.460
in the foreground.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.980
If you follow that reading, a peace-flavored visit does not pause the war, and continuing

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.780
to fight is presented as a rejection of a deal struck over Ukraine's head.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.380
The Guardian instead set Zelensky's words against earlier praise from United States envoy

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:54.380
Steve Whitkoff, for humanitarian gestures by Vladimir Putin.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:59.900
That paper organized the day as a rhetorical clash between Ukrainian leadership and American

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.040
diplomatic language, inside ongoing European coverage of the war.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.920
Follow that reading, and the argument is about the vocabulary great powers use while

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.860
fighting continues, not only about the blast sites.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.800
The two accounts share the day's order of events and still split on what to put first.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.620
The civilian toll or the fight over words.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:24.680
Neither one claims the conversation in the room rewrote orders already moving on the ground.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:30.400
Scheduled talks in mid-November among the United States, Russia, and Ukraine will now

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.960
either proceed or stall.

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:37.559
Tais' province in Yemen saw government forces carry out hundreds of strikes against positions

00:01:37.559 --> 00:01:42.399
held by the Houthi movement, an armed group fighting the internationally recognized government,

00:01:42.839 --> 00:01:44.979
while clashes continued in several districts.

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:50.459
The United Nations says almost 260,000 people have been displaced since August,

00:01:50.999 --> 00:01:56.039
with roughly half now sheltering in Tais. That is a very large movement of people into

00:01:56.039 --> 00:02:00.759
one province in a short span of months, and it is the figure aid planners are using.

00:02:01.539 --> 00:02:06.239
Al Jazeera described the government operations as targeting houthi gatherings and infrastructure,

00:02:06.899 --> 00:02:12.679
and noted verified civilian casualties, including many children. Humanitarian agencies have reached

00:02:12.679 --> 00:02:19.159
more than 174,000 displaced people with initial aid, according to that same account, which stays

00:02:19.159 --> 00:02:24.439
on the immediate military actions and the scale of civilian movement. It does not assign a broader

00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:29.899
strategic motive to either force. Aid groups will track whether shelter needs can be met while

00:02:29.899 --> 00:02:35.667
the fighting stays concentrated in the province. An attack on an airport in eastern Saudi Arabia

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:40.607
killed two people, Saudi authorities said, and they attributed the incident to the Houthi movement.

00:02:40.607 --> 00:02:46.267
That movement has carried out a series of similar strikes on Saudi targets, and BBC World

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:50.487
News presented the deaths as the latest in a pattern of operations against airports

00:02:50.487 --> 00:02:52.287
and other sites inside the kingdom.

00:02:52.927 --> 00:02:57.187
The report records those official statements and does not add claims about the attackers

00:02:57.187 --> 00:02:59.467
intentions or a wider regional war.

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:05.047
Saudi officials are expected to release further details on security measures at civilian facilities.

00:03:05.047 --> 00:03:11.361
Germany's export-led model faces pressure from Chinese competition, high energy prices

00:03:11.361 --> 00:03:17.521
and labor costs with real growth in gross domestic product or GDP, the broadest measure

00:03:17.521 --> 00:03:20.481
of output of only 0.2% last year.

00:03:21.261 --> 00:03:25.581
Deutschewelle reported that the government has identified six priority sectors for future

00:03:25.581 --> 00:03:30.681
growth, including artificial intelligence or AI and clean energy technologies.

00:03:30.681 --> 00:03:35.041
parties. Everything turns on whether that rebuild arrives faster than political support

00:03:35.041 --> 00:03:40.921
moves somewhere else. The far-right alternative for Germany party, or AFD, now leads opinion

00:03:40.921 --> 00:03:46.041
polls and has proposed ending the renewable energy transition, the shift away from fossil

00:03:46.041 --> 00:03:51.661
fuels, while restricting immigration. An advocate for that platform would say exporters cannot

00:03:51.661 --> 00:03:56.861
compete while energy and labor stay expensive, so cheaper power and tighter borders are the

00:03:56.861 --> 00:03:59.361
repair, not another industrial slogan.

00:03:59.821 --> 00:04:04.541
The strongest case for staying with new technology rests on a business initiative estimating

00:04:04.541 --> 00:04:08.961
up to 4.1 trillion euros in potential investment by 2035.

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:15.181
That sum is a projection of what new industries might attract, not money already spent, and

00:04:15.181 --> 00:04:19.541
the same coverage links weak performance to the party's rising support without predicting

00:04:19.541 --> 00:04:20.621
who will win an election.

00:04:20.621 --> 00:04:27.741
Government forecasts of 1.3% growth for 2026 will be compared against actual industrial

00:04:27.741 --> 00:04:28.661
output figures.

00:04:29.704 --> 00:04:35.724
Barclays announced plans to reduce its workforce by 5,000 positions or 5%, citing efficiency

00:04:35.724 --> 00:04:38.204
gains from greater use of artificial intelligence.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:43.624
The BBC carried the bank's statement that AI adoption is driving the cuts, and the public

00:04:43.624 --> 00:04:48.904
explanation on offer is efficiency savings rather than a wider claim about jobs across banking.

00:04:48.904 --> 00:04:49.004
marketing.

00:04:49.604 --> 00:04:53.324
Barclays will report the pace of the reductions in its next quarterly update.

00:04:54.173 --> 00:04:59.153
Physical prices for Brent Crude, a widely used grade of oil, have moved lower while

00:04:59.153 --> 00:05:03.933
futures prices have risen, creating a visible split between two benchmarks that usually

00:05:03.933 --> 00:05:04.793
travel together.

00:05:05.633 --> 00:05:10.073
Bloomberg described that split as unusual and noted that it is showing up in two closely

00:05:10.073 --> 00:05:15.393
washed versions of Brent, with market participants offering different readings of near-term supply,

00:05:15.393 --> 00:05:18.633
and no single cause pinned down beyond those assessments.

00:05:19.705 --> 00:05:24.865
Dodoma Region in Tanzania has enrolled 111,515 residents

00:05:24.865 --> 00:05:28.465
in universal health coverage through a government-supported program.

00:05:28.905 --> 00:05:33.065
Progress worth knowing for households that would otherwise face a sudden hospital bill.

00:05:33.725 --> 00:05:38.205
Regional Commissioner Rosemary Senyamele urged further sign-ups to shield families

00:05:38.205 --> 00:05:42.825
from unexpected medical costs. All Africa reported, keeping the focus

00:05:42.825 --> 00:05:46.725
on the concrete enrollment total and that local call for wider uptake.

00:05:47.285 --> 00:05:50.945
Officials will track whether enrollment continues to rise in the coming months.

00:05:51.963 --> 00:05:57.263
Elsewhere, flagship stores on the Champs-Alisee and Avenue Montagne in Paris have installed

00:05:57.263 --> 00:06:01.643
protective grates after weekend violence, the South China Morning Post reports.

00:06:02.383 --> 00:06:06.783
Chinese applicants for study in France say they will still proceed with visas and language

00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:08.403
programs despite the unrest.

00:06:08.403 --> 00:06:15.023
West. The world's largest wealth fund, Norway's, valued at around $2.3 trillion, recorded

00:06:15.023 --> 00:06:20.343
a $30 billion quarterly loss after bond market turbulence, CNBC states.

00:06:20.863 --> 00:06:26.043
A judge in New Mexico ordered meta to pay $25 billion after finding the company misled

00:06:26.043 --> 00:06:30.703
users about data handling linked to Cambridge Analytica, Al Jazeera reports.

00:06:31.403 --> 00:06:38.143
Mark Zuckerberg told investors third-quarter revenue reached $64.6 billion, a 26% rise,

00:06:38.583 --> 00:06:42.903
and that the Muse AI agent has 10 million users, according to France 24.

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:49.023
Investors move toward German buns, Germany's government buns, and United States treasuries

00:06:49.023 --> 00:06:51.923
amid rising French yields, Bloomberg reports.

00:06:52.503 --> 00:06:57.503
New permits have been issued for silver imports into India ahead of Diwali, the peak jewelry

00:06:57.503 --> 00:06:58.983
season, as Kerb's ease.

00:06:58.983 --> 00:07:05.043
India has invited bids for four amphibious warships, landing platform docs each exceeding

00:07:05.043 --> 00:07:08.343
30,000 tons, the South China Morning Post reports.

00:07:08.983 --> 00:07:14.443
A New York Times correspondent, recorded by France 24, described popular dissatisfaction

00:07:14.443 --> 00:07:20.143
across Europe over wages, housing, and political drift, saying promises of more economic growth

00:07:20.143 --> 00:07:21.123
have not come true.

00:07:21.703 --> 00:07:27.983
The Cali Fund, meant to raise $1 billion a year for biodiversity, has attracted just $7,000

00:07:27.983 --> 00:07:33.043
with the Guardian reporting almost nothing from drug companies and accusations that big

00:07:33.043 --> 00:07:38.043
pharma is free-writing on nature. To really understand how meetings between adversaries

00:07:38.043 --> 00:07:43.514
get arranged, look at the mandate, not the handshake. A common misunderstanding treats

00:07:43.514 --> 00:07:48.374
a single envoy visit as either a breakthrough or a betrayal, when the machinery underneath

00:07:48.374 --> 00:07:53.614
is more ordinary than either headline. Onvoys typically carry limited instructions set

00:07:53.614 --> 00:07:58.914
in advance by their governments, often after coordination with allies and military commanders,

00:07:59.354 --> 00:08:02.674
so the conversation in the room is bounded before anyone sits down.

00:08:03.274 --> 00:08:07.414
Because those instructions are already fixed, the meeting itself rarely changes battlefield

00:08:07.414 --> 00:08:09.234
orders that are already in motion.

00:08:09.934 --> 00:08:11.854
Historical parallels run the same way.

00:08:12.394 --> 00:08:17.354
Even when talks occur, each side continues operations until a written agreement is reached and then

00:08:17.354 --> 00:08:20.294
verified on the ground, not until a photo is released.

00:08:20.294 --> 00:08:23.374
That pattern is a calibration, not a forecast.

00:08:24.034 --> 00:08:26.694
It is how this channel has worked when it has worked at all.

00:08:27.194 --> 00:08:31.354
When you hear that one session opened the door to peace, or that it's signaled surrender,

00:08:31.954 --> 00:08:36.674
the firmer test is whether any written proposals were exchanged and whether forces on both sides

00:08:36.674 --> 00:08:37.814
receive new instructions.

00:08:38.494 --> 00:08:43.774
Joint communicates and verified casualty reports sit on firmer ground than the first wire summary,

00:08:44.274 --> 00:08:48.634
and reading outlets based in different regions is how you see which facts are shared and which

00:08:48.634 --> 00:08:49.654
are still disputed.

00:08:49.654 --> 00:08:54.414
The concrete thing to check is whether the next round still appears on official calendars

00:08:54.414 --> 00:08:55.914
after the most recent strikes.

00:08:56.893 --> 00:09:01.853
Al Jazeera organizes the same key day around civilian harm and a refusal of appeasement.

00:09:02.253 --> 00:09:07.053
The Guardian organizes it around Zellen's ski's mockery of American diplomatic language.

00:09:07.593 --> 00:09:12.393
The next weekly oil inventory report will show whether the gap between physical Brent barrels

00:09:12.393 --> 00:09:13.993
and crude futures narrows.

